export default {"P000084":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000084</code></p><h3>Absolutely flat ring</h3><p>Every module over the ring is flat.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/092F\">Stacks 092F · characterizations of absolute flatness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-092F\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/092B\">Stacks 092B · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-092B\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000084\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000089":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000089</code></p><h3>Artinian ring</h3><p>Every descending chain of ideals stabilizes.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00J5\">Stacks 00J5 · Artinian ring</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00J5\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000089\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000099":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000099</code></p><h3>Catenary ring</h3><p>For each pair of nested primes there is a finite bound on chain lengths between them, and all maximal chains between them have the same length.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NI\">Stacks 00NI · catenary ring</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00NI\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000099\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000091":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000091</code></p><h3>Coherent ring</h3><p>Every finitely generated ideal is a finitely presented module over the ring.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05CV\">Stacks 05CV · coherent ring · Stacks 05CV · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-05CV\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05CY\">Stacks 05CY · Noetherian implies coherent</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-05CY\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000091\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000029":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Schemes · predicate · <code>P000029</code></p><h3>Connected</h3><p>The underlying space is nonempty and admits no partition into two nonempty disjoint opens.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/004S\">Stacks 004S · connected spaces and their components</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-004S\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000029\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000082":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000082</code></p><h3>Connected prime spectrum</h3><p>The spectrum is nonempty and has no separation into two nonempty opens.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00EF\">Stacks 00EF · connected spectrum and idempotents</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00EF\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/004S\">Stacks 004S · nonempty connected spaces</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-004S\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000082\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000003":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P000003</code></p><h3>Étale</h3><p>Smooth of relative dimension zero; equivalently flat, unramified and locally of finite presentation.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02GH\">Stacks 02GH · étale morphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02GH\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-658-43031-3_3\">U. Görtz and T. Wedhorn, Algebraic Geometry II, Definition 18.34 and Theorem 18.44, including local finite presentation</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02GI\">Stacks 02GI · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02GI\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0259\">Stacks 0259 · common source definition · Stacks 0259 · (2) at all points</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/etale/#tag-0259\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000003\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000077":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000077</code></p><h3>Field</h3><p>The ring is nonzero and every nonzero element has a multiplicative inverse.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09FD\">Stacks 09FD · field and subfield · Stacks 09FD · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/fields/#tag-09FD\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000077\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000086":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000086</code></p><h3>Field at every prime</h3><p>For every prime ideal <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔭</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the local ring <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔭</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{\\mathfrak p}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is a field.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/092F\">Stacks 092F · characterizations of absolute flatness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-092F\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000086\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000019":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P000019</code></p><h3>Finite</h3><p>Affine, with every corresponding coordinate algebra finite as a module over the base ring.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WG\">Stacks 01WG · finite and integral morphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WG\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WH\">Stacks 01WH · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WH\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000019\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000098":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000098</code></p><h3>Finite global dimension</h3><p>There is a finite bound on the projective dimensions of all modules over the ring.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OE\">Stacks 00OE · finite global dimension and finite dimensional regularity</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00OE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00O6\">Stacks 00O6 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00O6\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000098\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000097":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000097</code></p><h3>Finite Krull dimension</h3><p>A finite integer bounds the lengths of chains of strict prime-ideal inclusions.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GIE\">Stacks 0GIE · chains of prime ideals</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0GIE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KE\">Stacks 00KE · Krull dimension</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KG\">Stacks 00KG · Krull dimension and prime heights</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KG\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000097\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000090":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000090</code></p><h3>Finite length over itself</h3><p>The ring as a module over itself has a finite composition series. The zero module has length zero.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00IU\">Stacks 00IU · length of a module</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00IU\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00JB\">Stacks 00JB · Artinian rings and length</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00JB\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000090\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000092":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000092</code></p><h3>Finitely many minimal primes</h3><p>The set of prime ideals minimal under inclusion is finite.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00FR\">Stacks 00FR · Noetherian rings have finitely many minimal primes</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00FR\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000092\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000093":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000093</code></p><h3>Finitely many prime ideals</h3><p>The underlying set of the prime spectrum is finite.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ALV\">Stacks 0ALV · finite prime spectrum of a Noetherian ring</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0ALV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000093\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000006":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P000006</code></p><h3>Flat</h3><p>For a morphism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and every <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the stalk <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal O_{X,x}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is flat as an <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal O_{Y,f(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-module. On affine charts this is equivalent to exactness of extension of scalars along the coordinate ring map.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01U2\">Stacks 01U2 · flat morphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01U2\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-658-30733-2_15\">U. Görtz and T. Wedhorn, Algebraic Geometry I, second edition, Definition 14.1(1),(3), stalks of the structure sheaf</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01U3\">Stacks 01U3 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01U3\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0253\">Stacks 0253 · common source definition · Stacks 0253 · (3) flat at every point</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/etale/#tag-0253\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000006\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000037":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Schemes · compound · <code>P000037</code></p><h3>Integral</h3><p>A scheme is integral when it is nonempty and every nonempty affine open has an integral domain as its coordinate ring. Equivalently it is reduced and irreducible.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OK\">Stacks 01OK · affine-local definition of an integral scheme · Stacks 01OK · numbered source statement · Stacks 01OK · nonempty scheme with domains on all nonempty affine opens</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/properties/#tag-01OK\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OJ\">Stacks 01OJ · integral schemes</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/properties/#tag-01OJ\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://hoyois.app.uni-regensburg.de/SS26/alggeo2/script.pdf#page=80\">M. Hoyois, Algebraic Geometry, 23 September 2026, Definition 8.43 and Example 8.44</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000037\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000078":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000078</code></p><h3>Integral domain</h3><p>The ring is nonzero and a product of two nonzero elements is nonzero.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09FE\">Stacks 09FE · integral domain</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/fields/#tag-09FE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00B2\">Stacks 00B2 · basic notions</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00B2\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000078\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000083":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000083</code></p><h3>Jacobson ring</h3><p>Each radical ideal is the intersection of the maximal ideals containing it.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00G0\">Stacks 00G0 · Jacobson ring</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00G0\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00G2\">Stacks 00G2 · prime-ideal criterion for Jacobson rings</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00G2\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000083\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000095":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000095</code></p><h3>Krull dimension at most one</h3><p>No chain of prime ideals contains two consecutive strict inclusions.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GIE\">Stacks 0GIE · chains of prime ideals</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0GIE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KE\">Stacks 00KE · Krull dimension</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KG\">Stacks 00KG · Krull dimension and prime heights</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KG\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000095\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000094":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000094</code></p><h3>Krull dimension at most zero</h3><p>There are no strict inclusions between prime ideals. Equivalently every prime ideal is maximal. This condition holds for the zero ring.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GIE\">Stacks 0GIE · chains of prime ideals</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0GIE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KE\">Stacks 00KE · Krull dimension</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KG\">Stacks 00KG · Krull dimension and prime heights</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KG\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000094\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000096":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000096</code></p><h3>Krull dimension exactly one</h3><p>Prime chains have at most one strict inclusion, and a strict inclusion of prime ideals occurs.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GIE\">Stacks 0GIE · chains of prime ideals</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0GIE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KE\">Stacks 00KE · Krull dimension</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00KG\">Stacks 00KG · Krull dimension and prime heights</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00KG\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000096\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000080":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000080</code></p><h3>Local ring</h3><p>The ring has exactly one maximal ideal.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07BI\">Stacks 07BI · local ring, residue field and local homomorphism · Stacks 07BI · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-07BI\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000080\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000036":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Schemes · compound · <code>P000036</code></p><h3>Noetherian</h3><p>Has a finite open affine cover by spectra of Noetherian rings.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OU\">Stacks 01OU · Noetherian schemes</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/properties/#tag-01OU\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://hoyois.app.uni-regensburg.de/SS26/alggeo2/script.pdf#page=78\">M. Hoyois, Algebraic Geometry, 23 September 2026, Definition 8.26</a> · <a href=\"https://hoyois.app.uni-regensburg.de/SS26/alggeo2/script.pdf#page=69\">M. Hoyois, Algebraic Geometry, 23 September 2026, Proposition 7.37, finite affine subcovers</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OV\">Stacks 01OV · common source definition · Stacks 01OV · (2)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/properties/#tag-01OV\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000036\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000088":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000088</code></p><h3>Noetherian ring</h3><p>Every ideal is finitely generated. Equivalently, every ascending chain of ideals stabilizes.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00B4\">Stacks 00B4 · Noetherian rings in the basic notions</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00B4\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00FM\">Stacks 00FM · definition and ascending-chain criterion</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00FM\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000088\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000066":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Schemes · predicate · <code>P000066</code></p><h3>Noetherian underlying space</h3><p>The Zariski space is Noetherian as a topological space. This condition alone does not require any affine coordinate ring to be Noetherian.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OZ\">Stacks 01OZ · Noetherian schemes have Noetherian spaces</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/properties/#tag-01OZ\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0050\">Stacks 0050 · Noetherian topological spaces</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-0050\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000066\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000076":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000076</code></p><h3>Nonzero ring</h3><p>The identities <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> are distinct.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00AQ\">Stacks 00AQ · zero-ring convention</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00AQ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000076\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000026":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · compound · <code>P000026</code></p><h3>Of finite type</h3><p>Locally of finite type and quasi-compact.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01T0\">Stacks 01T0 · morphisms of finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01T0\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000026\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000055":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces · predicate · <code>P000055</code></p><h3>Profinite space</h3><p>A cofiltered inverse limit of finite discrete spaces. Equivalently, quasi-compact, Hausdorff and totally disconnected.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08ZY\">Stacks 08ZY · characterization of profinite spaces</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-08ZY\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08ZX\">Stacks 08ZX · finite discrete limit definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-08ZX\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000055\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000052":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces · predicate · <code>P000052</code></p><h3>Quasi-compact space</h3><p>Every open cover admits a finite subcover.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0059\">Stacks 0059 · quasi-compact spaces</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-0059\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/005A\">Stacks 005A · common source definition · Stacks 005A · (1)</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-005A\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000052\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000013":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Schemes · predicate · <code>P000013</code></p><h3>Reduced</h3><p>All stalks have zero nilradical; equivalently every affine coordinate ring is reduced.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01IZ\">Stacks 01IZ · reduced schemes</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01IZ\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://hoyois.app.uni-regensburg.de/SS26/alggeo2/script.pdf#page=77\">M. Hoyois, Algebraic Geometry, 23 September 2026, Definition 8.13 and Proposition 8.15, affine-local criterion</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01J0\">Stacks 01J0 · numbered source statement · Stacks 01J0 · reduced stalks</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01J0\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000013\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000079":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000079</code></p><h3>Reduced ring</h3><p>An element whose positive power is zero must itself be zero.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00B3\">Stacks 00B3 · reduced rings</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00B3\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00EU\">Stacks 00EU · localization at a minimal prime</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00EU\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00EW\">Stacks 00EW · embedding in products of fields</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00EW\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000079\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000011":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Schemes · predicate · <code>P000011</code></p><h3>Regular</h3><p>Locally Noetherian and every local ring is regular: its dimension equals the minimal number of generators of its maximal ideal.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02IR\">Stacks 02IR · regular schemes</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/properties/#tag-02IR\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02IS\">Stacks 02IS · Noetherian regular affine neighbourhoods</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/properties/#tag-02IS\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000011\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000081":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000081</code></p><h3>Semilocal ring</h3><p>The set of maximal ideals of the ring is finite.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03C0\">Stacks 03C0 · semilocal ring</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-03C0\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000081\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000056":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Topological spaces · predicate · <code>P000056</code></p><h3>Spectral space</h3><p>A sober, quasi-compact space with a basis of quasi-compact opens and with their pairwise intersections quasi-compact.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08YF\">Stacks 08YF · spectral spaces and the constructible topology</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-08YF\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://api.pageplace.de/preview/DT0400.9781108609586_A36703407/preview-9781108609586_A36703407.pdf#page=24\">Dickmann, Schwartz &amp; Tressl, Spectral Spaces, Definition 1.1.5. The four spectral axioms include unique generic points for nonempty irreducible closed sets.</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08YG\">Stacks 08YG · common source definition · Stacks 08YG · spectral space</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/topology/#tag-08YG\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000056\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000040":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Morphisms of schemes · predicate · <code>P000040</code></p><h3>Universally open</h3><p>After every base change the map sends opens to opens.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UA\">Stacks 01UA · flat morphisms locally of finite presentation are universally open</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01UA\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://hoyois.app.uni-regensburg.de/SS26/alggeo2/script.pdf#page=55\">M. Hoyois, Algebraic Geometry, 23 September 2026, Definition 5.32 and Proposition 5.33(i), after arbitrary base change</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01U0\">Stacks 01U0 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01U0\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000040\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000087":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000087</code></p><h3>Valuation ring at every prime</h3><p>For every prime ideal <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔭</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak p</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the local ring <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔭</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{\\mathfrak p}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is a valuation ring.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/092S\">Stacks 092S · characterizations of weak dimension at most one</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-092S\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000087\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","P000085":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · predicate · <code>P000085</code></p><h3>Weak dimension at most one</h3><p>Every module over the ring has flat dimension at most one. Equivalently, every ideal of the ring is flat as a module.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/092D\">Stacks 092D · weak dimension</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-092D\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/092S\">Stacks 092S · characterizations of weak dimension at most one</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/more-algebra/#tag-092S\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../topologies/database/#P000085\">Open shared record</a></p></article>"};
